    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the price per ounce of John's M&M purchase? John buys 3 large bags of M&M weighing 12 ounces each. Each large bag of M&M weighs 10 ounces.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 6; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many small bags of M&M can John make? Also, here's some relevant info: John puts 10 M&M in each small bag.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"John has:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n3 \\\\times 10 = 30\\\\text{ ounces}\\n\\\\]\\n\\nWith 32 M&M per ounce:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n30 \\\\times 32 = 960\\\\text{ M&M}\\n\\\\]\\n\\nPutting 10 M&M in each small bag:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n960 \\\\div 10 = 96\\n\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{96\\\\text{ smal...\n- {\"content\":\"Here's another detail: John pays $0.40 per ounce for the M&M bags.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"John buys a total of:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n3 \\\\times 10 = 30\\\\text{ ounces}\\n\\\\]\\n\\nAt \\\\(\\\\$0.40\\\\) per ounce:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n30 \\\\times \\\\$0.40 = \\\\$12.00\\n\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\\\$12.00}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Each ounce of M&M contains 30 M&M.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The number of M&M candies per ounce does not affect the price per ounce.\n\nJohn pays **$0.40 for each ounce**, so the price per ounce is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$0.40\\text{ per ounce}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
